        "alt": "AKU declared best compliant employer in Pakistan"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Aga Khan University (AKU) was declared the \"Best Compliant Employer\" for the year 2002-2003, by the Employees' Old-Age Benefits Institution (EOBI), Pakistan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "In addition, the criteria for achieving the First Excellence Award of EOBI included availability of complete records of all employees; willingness in the execution of amendments in EOBI Act; and no instances of indulgence in litigation or fine for late payments.The award was presented to Mr. Navroz Surani, Director of Human Resources at AKU, at the EOBI's first \"Excellence Award\" ceremony held at Avari Towers, in Karachi. AKU was selected as the 'Best Employer' from amongst the 48,000 organisations registered with EOBI, for being the most efficient organisation in fulfilling the requirements of EOBI registration, contribution/claims and submission of returns in a timely manner."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
